Movement regression tests: ramp data path + drone re-attack.

Proves the tilt pipeline end to end short of rasterization: real-map TMP
headers carry SlopeIndex 1..18 (verified with a mix probe on Hills.mmx
and Valley.mmx), arm_land_speed delivers them through ramp_at, and
slope_tilt_pitch returns nonzero pitch aligned with the slope axis (zero
on flat ground). Plus a terror-drone loop test: infect, damage ticks,
eject on host death, re-infect a second host (incl. the 3xROF post-eject
freeze). No engine change; no save-format change.

--- a/tests/test_slope_tilt.cpp
+++ b/tests/test_slope_tilt.cpp
@@ -1,6 +1,9 @@
 #include "doctest.h"
 #include "slope_tilt.hpp"
+#include "asset_fixture.hpp"
+#include "world.hpp"
 #include <cmath>
+#include <vector>
 
 TEST_CASE("slope_tilt: flat SlopeIndex is zero pitch") {
     CHECK(ra2engine::slope_tilt_pitch(0, 0) == 0.0);
@@ -23,3 +26,27 @@
     const double p = ra2engine::slope_tilt_pitch(4, 0x4000);
